{
	"_readme": [
		"Date and time built-ins: DATE DATEDIF DATEVALUE DAY DAYS EDATE EOMONTH HOUR",
		"MINUTE MONTH NETWORKDAYS NOW SECOND TIME TIMEVALUE TODAY WEEKDAY WORKDAY YEAR.",
		"",
		"Two conventions used throughout this file.",
		"",
		"1. Date literals are written as 'YYYY-MM-DD 00:00:00', not 'YYYY-MM-DD'.",
		"   The engine parses every date with `new Date(string)`, then reads the",
		"   result with LOCAL getters. A bare ISO date is parsed as UTC midnight, so",
		"   DAY('2026-05-23') is 23 east of Greenwich and 22 west of it. The",
		"   space-separated form is parsed as local time, which makes the fixture",
		"   answer the same in every time zone. The time-zone leak itself is covered",
		"   in formula.functions.lookup.test.ts, which can assert it deterministically.",
		"",
		"2. This engine represents a date as an ISO string, not as an Excel serial",
		"   number. Fixtures whose only difference from Excel is that representation",
		"   carry source 'engine-contract' and name the Excel serial in notes. The",
		"   consequences of the choice - date arithmetic, date comparison, dates in",
		"   ranges - are recorded as known-failures, because those produce wrong",
		"   answers rather than a different-looking right one.",
		"",
		"Wrong-argument-count cases use Google Sheets as the oracle: Sheets surfaces",
		"'Wrong number of arguments' as #N/A, while Excel refuses the formula at entry",
		"and so has no value to compare against."
	],
